# TECHO5 daemon as an init service on LineageOS (the Echo Spot, rook; the same service as the Show's).
#
# Install (root, /system remounted rw):
#   cp bin/echod-arm-spot /system/bin/techo5 && chmod 755 /system/bin/techo5
#   chcon u:object_r:system_file:s0 /system/bin/techo5
#   cp tools/init/techo5.rc /system/etc/init/techo5.rc
#
# The binary lives on /system so init execs a system_file and the service runs in init's own
# domain, which on this permissive build is what reaches /dev/snd and the input devices. The
# state directory is on /data. Android's audio stack must be on the null HAL
# (ro.hardware.audio.primary=default) or audioserver will fight over the PCM devices.

on post-fs-data
    mkdir /data/misc/techo5 0700 root root
    mkdir /data/misc/techo5/models 0755 root root
    mkdir /data/techo5 0755 root root

# Not oneshot: the daemon exits on purpose after installing an update and expects init to start
# it again into the new binary, and a crash should come back too. init backs off if it keeps dying.
service techo5 /system/bin/techo5 run
    class late_start
    user root
    group root audio input system
    disabled

# Start once the framework is up, so the AFE and the Wi-Fi are settled and audioserver has
# already opened (and, on the null HAL, not touched) its devices.
on property:sys.boot_completed=1
    start techo5
